\lispPackageChapter{chorus/api/memory}

This package allocates device memory, host memory, and memory blocks that
pair the two. \texttt{chorus/api} reexports it.

\section{Memory blocks}

\lispFunctionSubsection{alloc-memory-block}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(alloc-memory-block \lispVar{type} \lispVar{size})}

Allocates a block of \texttt{size} elements of \texttt{type}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{free-memory-block}

Frees both the device pointer and the host pointer of a block.

\lispMacroSubsection{with-memory-block}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(with-memory-block (\lispVar{var} \lispVar{type} \lispVar{size})
  \&body \lispVar{body})}

Binds \texttt{var} to a new block and frees it on the way out.

\lispMacroSubsection{with-memory-blocks}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(with-memory-blocks \lispVar{bindings} \&body \lispVar{body})}

Each binding has the form \texttt{(\lispVar{var} \lispVar{type} \lispVar{size})}.
The macro nests \texttt{with-memory-block}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{sync-memory-block}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(sync-memory-block \lispVar{memory-block} \lispVar{direction})}

\texttt{direction} is \texttt{:host-to-device} or \texttt{:device-to-host}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{memory-block-aref}

\lispSyntax

\texttt{(memory-block-aref \lispVar{memory-block} \lispVar{index})}

Reads the host side of the block. \texttt{setf} writes it. A copy to or from
the device is a separate \texttt{sync-memory-block} call.

The package also exports \texttt{memory-block-p},
\texttt{memory-block-device-ptr}, \texttt{memory-block-host-ptr},
\texttt{memory-block-type}, and \texttt{memory-block-size}.

\section{Separate host and device memory}

\texttt{alloc-device-memory} takes a type and a count.
\texttt{free-device-memory} frees that pointer.
\texttt{with-device-memory} has the form
\texttt{(with-device-memory (\lispVar{var} \lispVar{type} \lispVar{n}) \&body \lispVar{body})}.

\texttt{alloc-host-memory}, \texttt{free-host-memory}, and
\texttt{host-memory-aref} are the host-side counterparts.
\texttt{with-host-memory} has the same form as \texttt{with-device-memory}.

\texttt{memcpy-host-to-device} and \texttt{memcpy-device-to-host} copy a
region. \texttt{device-total-bytes}, \texttt{device-total-kbytes},
\texttt{device-total-mbytes}, and \texttt{device-total-gbytes} report the
memory on a device. \texttt{device-total-bytes} takes the device as its
argument.
